# Agent commit partition

When planning or landing multi-file feature work (especially Cursor-coauthored):

## Required phase order

1. Types / API clients (+ delete legacy clients if retiring)  
2. Pure utils / projections + unit tests  
3. Forms / tables / hooks  
4. Reports registry / menu defs / print builders  
5. Pages/tab wiring + e2e mocks  
6. Docs / Cursor rules / ADRs (last)

## Agent response duty

Before implementing a large change, outline this partition. Refuse a plan that is a single megacommit mixing phases 1–6.

When the user asks to commit, split along these phases (see also `commit-cadence.mdc`).
